  "final_text": "**Your last 3 weeks of sleep (26 Feb to 18 Mar) look fair on duration, but the quality data looks unreliable.**\n\n**Duration**\n- You averaged about 7.0 hours a night over 21 nights. The range was 5.7 to 8.1 hours.\n- Your longest nights were 3 Mar (8.1 h), 10 Mar (8.0 h) and 2 Mar (7.9 h).\n- Your shortest were 17 Mar (5.7 h) and 7 Mar (5.9 h). These were the only two nights under 6 hours.\n- The last three nights ran short: 6.2 h, 5.7 h and 6.25 h. That is a small sleep debt building right now.\n\n**Sleep stages**\n- You got roughly 17% deep sleep, 63% light and 20% REM. Those proportions barely moved from night to night.\n- Each night had about 13 minutes awake, in 2 wakeups.\n\n**Quality metrics**\n- 20 of the 21 nights have identical values:\n  - sleep score 63 (Fair)\n  - overnight HRV 61\n  - sleep stress 19\n  - SpO2 average 94% and low 87%\n- Real data doesn't normally repeat this exactly. These numbers may be placeholders or a sync problem, so I wouldn't read anything into the score or HRV trend for that period.\n- Only today's night (18 Mar) looks like a real reading:\n  - score 74 (Fair)\n  - HRV 58\n  - sleep stress 14\n  - SpO2 average 95%\n  - deep sleep 18.7%\n  - 26 minutes awake\n- Today's night is also short, at 6.25 hours.\n\n**Takeaway:** You're getting about 7 hours on average, with a dip this week. If you have a hard session planned, an easier day or an earlier night would help. I can check today's readiness and HRV trend if you'd like. It might also be worth checking that your watch is syncing properly.",
